-That's awesome.

2199
01:24:49,350 --> 01:24:51,653
-That was so cool.
-All right, then.

2200
01:24:51,719 --> 01:24:54,022
Press one for Yong-wook and two for Poong.

2201
01:24:54,089 --> 01:24:55,023
Press one!

2202
01:24:56,191 --> 01:24:57,525
-He pressed one.
-He decides quickly.

2203
01:24:57,592 --> 01:25:00,228
And now, let's find out
who J. Y. Park chose!

2204
01:25:00,295 --> 01:25:01,296
Show us!

2205
01:25:02,097 --> 01:25:05,166
Not half air, half sound,
but Half Pork, Half Kimchi!

2206
01:25:05,233 --> 01:25:08,136
A dish that comforted his heart.

2207
01:25:08,203 --> 01:25:10,305
Was it Poong's plastic pants?

2208
01:25:10,371 --> 01:25:12,907
Or was it Yong-wook's smoked dishes?

2209
01:25:12,974 --> 01:25:13,975
I can't tell.

2210
01:25:14,042 --> 01:25:17,145
Who did J. Y. Park choose?

2211
01:25:17,212 --> 01:25:19,080
-Who won?
-Who did he choose?

2212
01:25:21,950 --> 01:25:23,451
YOO YONG-WOOK WINS

2213
01:25:23,518 --> 01:25:24,919
DIRECTOR YOO YONG-WOOK'S SEYP WINS

2214
01:25:24,986 --> 01:25:26,788
Director Yong-wook wins.

2215
01:25:26,855 --> 01:25:28,957
-Great job.
-Thank you.

2216
01:25:29,023 --> 01:25:31,059
Thank you.

2217
01:25:32,293 --> 01:25:34,095
BEATS THE GATEKEEPER
AND CLAIMS HIS FIRST WIN

2218
01:25:34,162 --> 01:25:36,531
No matter how delicious his dish is,

2219
01:25:36,598 --> 01:25:40,001
I thought the act of smoking the food
was a bit unrelated to Korean cuisine

2220
01:25:40,068 --> 01:25:42,704
and wouldn't go well with the food.

2221
01:25:42,770 --> 01:25:45,006
But it had a surprising effect

2222
01:25:45,073 --> 01:25:49,377
<i>of bringing out more Korean flavors</i>
<i>from the ingredients.</i>

2223
01:25:50,245 --> 01:25:52,480
That was shocking.

2224
01:25:52,547 --> 01:25:54,449
I'm a bit dazed right now.

2225
01:25:54,516 --> 01:25:57,919
I have done everything
I possibly could today,

2226
01:25:57,986 --> 01:26:02,624
so it's just a wonder
how you come up with new ideas every week.

2227
01:26:02,690 --> 01:26:04,926
I have so much respect for everyone.

2228
01:26:04,993 --> 01:26:06,194
I see.

2229
01:26:07,095 --> 01:26:09,063
May I leave a word for Poong?

2230
01:26:09,130 --> 01:26:12,233
This idea itself was impossible.

2231
01:26:12,300 --> 01:26:15,503
As I mentioned before,
the plastic pants proved

2232
01:26:15,570 --> 01:26:19,574
that his cooking skills
should not be taken too lightly.

2233
01:26:19,641 --> 01:26:21,543
She said that's how you make
Chinese starch sheets.

2234
01:26:21,609 --> 01:26:23,311
Thank you very much.

2235
01:26:23,378 --> 01:26:27,282
You must be quite disappointed.
The plastic pants turned out so well.

2236
01:26:27,348 --> 01:26:28,850
I'm fine.

2237
01:26:28,917 --> 01:26:32,820
I had tons of fun today.

2238
01:26:32,887 --> 01:26:35,056
So yes, it was fun.

2239
01:26:35,523 --> 01:26:38,259
THE PLASTIC PANTS WILL GO DOWN IN HISTORY

2240
01:26:38,326 --> 01:26:39,160
They were both cool.

2241
01:26:39,594 --> 01:26:43,097
YOO YONG-WOOK TAKES HIS FIRST STAR

2242
01:26:43,398 --> 01:26:46,434
-He wins his debut match! Congrats!
-Congratulations.

2243
01:26:46,501 --> 01:26:48,503
COMING UP: PREVIEW FOR
UHM JUNG-HWA & SOOYOUNG'S EPISODE

2244
01:26:49,070 --> 01:26:50,271
TODAY'S FRIDGE OWNERS

2245
01:26:50,572 --> 01:26:52,907
CHOI SOOYOUNG & UHM JUNG-HWA

2246
01:26:52,974 --> 01:26:54,242
That's what I'm talking about.

2247
01:26:54,309 --> 01:26:55,410
I can't look at her.

2248
01:26:55,476 --> 01:26:56,611
What are you doing?

2249
01:26:56,678 --> 01:26:57,946
Everything he says sounds like a lie.

2250
01:26:58,246 --> 01:26:59,214
ON TOP OF THAT

2251
01:26:59,280 --> 01:27:01,416
-You probably weren't a huge fan.
-Me?

2252
01:27:01,482 --> 01:27:02,951
What's my debut project?

2253
01:27:03,017 --> 01:27:04,285
I forgot the title.

2254
01:27:04,586 --> 01:27:05,920
HIS TRUE COLORS FINALLY SHOW

2255
01:27:05,987 --> 01:27:08,089
His credibility just dropped.

2256
01:27:08,156 --> 01:27:09,457
She's now suspicious of Sung-jun.

2257
01:27:09,657 --> 01:27:10,692
TO CAPTURE SOOYOUNG'S HEART,

2258
01:27:10,758 --> 01:27:12,961
THE CHEFS DEPLOY DIFFERENT STRATEGIES

2259
01:27:13,428 --> 01:27:15,263
SHAKING HIS HEAD VIOLENTLY

2260
01:27:15,563 --> 01:27:16,397
TASTE OF HER OWN MEDICINE

2261
01:27:16,631 --> 01:27:17,498
ENERGY!

2262
01:27:17,899 --> 01:27:18,900
MAKING AN IMPRESSION

2263
01:27:18,967 --> 01:27:20,068
She's addicted to dancing.

2264
01:27:20,134 --> 01:27:22,070
-What are you up to?
-Go away!

2265
01:27:22,337 --> 01:27:24,172
I'LL SHOW YOU WHAT I CAN REALLY DO!

2266
01:27:24,439 --> 01:27:25,907
RISKING EVERYTHING TO LOOK COOL

2267
01:27:26,341 --> 01:27:27,342
OH, MY GOSH

2268
01:27:27,575 --> 01:27:29,410
DID IT WORK?

2269
01:27:30,712 --> 01:27:31,746
IS THERE A PROBLEM?

2270
01:27:33,948 --> 01:27:35,817
WHICH CHEF WILL SHE CHOOSE?

2271
01:27:35,883 --> 01:27:37,719
<i>You had us scared there.</i>

2272
01:27:39,354 --> 01:27:41,556
I've always dreamed
of this moment since childhood.

2273
01:27:41,623 --> 01:27:42,824
"Into the New World" with her.

2274
01:27:42,890 --> 01:27:43,758
I decline.

2275
01:27:45,560 --> 01:27:46,861
We also don't want to see it.

2276
01:27:56,504 --> 01:28:01,276
Subtitle translation by: Eunsook Youn
